  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list prepared under RBC-RAD-07. Four studies are booked. appt-00006, -00001 and -00008 were cancelled, so I placed no orders for them.\n\n1. pt-0047 Mohr, 08:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0001). No contrast reaction on record. He has diabetes (diet only), and his last creatinine (9/24) was outside 30 days, so I ordered a creatinine to be drawn before the scan (sr-t0009). Instructions sent (comm-t0011). A later outside result showed creatinine 1.52 on 10/22, up from 0.94 (eGFR 64). It doesn't meet the policy's AKI criteria, because the rise happened over 28 days, not within 7. No IV fluids are needed and the decision stands. I made a follow-up task for you about the rising trend (task-t0027).\n\n2. pt-0015 Ferreira, 09:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0002). The 2019 report from the day of the reaction grades it as moderate (the allergy list says anaphylaxis by patient report, which doesn't change the grade). Premedication ordered: prednisone 50 mg at 10/25 20:00, 10/26 02:00 and 08:00 (mr-t0005), plus diphenhydramine 50 mg at 08:00 (mr-t0006). After I started, the lab corrected his 10/14 creatinine from 0.98 to 2.8 (the first value was another patient's sample), so his eGFR is 24. I added IV saline 500 mL starting at 08:00 (mr-t0016). He got instructions and then a corrected message, both in Spanish and English (comm-t0012, comm-t0020): needs a driver, arrive at 08:00. Kidney follow-up task for you (task-t0026).\n\n3. pt-0049 Schuster, 13:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast (sr-t0003). She had AKI on 10/4 and her creatinine has not been shown back to baseline. Ordered: creatinine drawn before the scan (sr-t0010), IV saline 500 mL at 12:00 (mr-t0007), and a hold on metformin (mr-00392) from the scan day through 48 h after, restarting only once her kidney function is rechecked and normal (task-t0015). An outside report that arrived during the work shows a moderate reaction to iopamidol in 2022. She had told the phone screen \"no,\" but the report governs, so I added premedication: prednisone 50 mg at 00:00, 06:00 and 12:00 (mr-t0017) plus diphenhydramine 50 mg at 12:00 (mr-t0018). Instructions plus an update sent (comm-t0013, comm-t0021): needs a driver. Iopamidol still needs adding to her allergy list; there was no catalog code to record it.\n\n4. pt-0046 Beahan, 14:00, CT abdomen/pelvis without contrast, stone protocol (sr-t0004). No prep needed; she was told (comm-t0014). An outside report showed a mild iohexol reaction in 2024, which I added to her allergy list (alg-t0019). It doesn't affect this scan.\n\nI signed a prep note for each patient and closed the four inbox items that came in during the work. Your other inbox items were left untouched.",
